\pard\f2\b\fs28\fi-1020\li1200\fc0\cf0 Description\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\f0\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 The NSDraggingSource informal protocol declares methods that are implemented by the source object in a dragging session (see the NSDraggingDestination protocol for definitions of dragging terms). The 
\i dragging source 
\i0 is specified as an argument to the 
\b dragImage:at:offset:event:pasteboard:source:slideBack: 
\b0 message, sent to a window or view object to initiate the dragging session. \

\fs14 \

\fs28 See the documentation of the 
\b dragImage:...
\b0  method in NSView for a warning regarding the mouse-down event that initiates a dragging session.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 Of the methods declared below, only 
\b draggingSourceOperationMaskForLocal:
\b0  must be implemented. The other methods are invoked only if the dragging source implements them. All four methods are invoked automatically during a dragging session–you never send an NSDraggingSource message directly to an object.\

\fs14 \

\fs56 \

