{\pard\tx8260\f2\b\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0{\NeXTHelpMarker2856 \markername NS_DEV_DOCFOR:objc_method:[NSDraggingSource-draggingSourceOperationMaskForLocal:];}
¨}\pard\tx8260\f2\b\i0\ulnone\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 draggingSourceOperationMaskForLocal:\

\fs6 \

\pard\f1\b0\fs28\fi-620\li2520\fc0\cf0 -
\f0  (unsigned int)
\b draggingSourceOperationMaskForLocal:
\b0 (BOOL)
\i flag\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\i0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 This is the only NSDraggingSource method that must be implemented by the source object. It should return a mask, built by combining the applicable constants listed below using the C bitwise OR operator. You should use this mask to indicate which types of dragging operations the source object will allow to be performed on the dragged image's data. A YES value for
\i  flag
\i0  indicates that the candidate destination object (the window or view over which the dragged image is currently poised) is in the same application as the source, while a NO value indicates that the destination object is in a different application.\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx6740\tx9540\f2\b\fs28\li1900\fc0\cf0 Option	Meaning\

\fs6 \

\pard\tx6740\tx9520\f0\b0\fs28\fi-4840\li6740\fc0\cf0 NSDragOperationCopy	The data represented by the image can be copied.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSDragOperationLink	The data can be shared.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSDragOperationGeneric	The operation can be defined by the destination.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSDragOperationPrivate	The operation is negotiated privately between the source and the destination.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 NSDragOperationAll	Combines all the above.\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 If the source does not permit any dragging operations, then it should return NSDragOperationNone.\

\fs14 \

\fs46 \

{\pard\tx8260\f2\b\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0{\NeXTHelpMarker4026 \markername NS_DEV_DOCFOR:objc_method:[NSDraggingSource-ignoreModifierKeysWhileDragging];}
¨}\pard\tx8260\f2\b\i0\ulnone\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 ignoreModifierKeysWhileDragging\

\fs6 \

\pard\f1\b0\fs28\fi-620\li2520\fc0\cf0 -
\f0  (BOOL)
\b ignoreModifierKeysWhileDragging\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 Sets whether the use of the modifier keys should have no effect on the type of operation performed. If this method is not implemented or returns NO, then the user can tailor the drag operation by holding down a modifier key during the drag. The dragging option that corresponds to the modifier key is combined with the source's mask (as set with the 
\b draggingSourceOperationMaskForLocal:
\b0  method) using the C bitwise AND operator. See the description for the 
\b draggingSourceOperationMask
\b0  method in the NSDraggingInfo protocol specification for more information about dragging masks and modifier keys.\

\fs14 \

